[Term]
id: RTO:0000001
name: collimator
def: "A device that limits the 2D spatial extent of the fluence of subatomic particles." []
is_a: OBI:0000968

[Term]
id: RTO:0000002
name: radiation source
def: "A device that has been constructed so as to emit subatomic particles." []
comment: Radiation source refers to the device that actually produces the radiation independent of the application to radiation therapy.  For example, a linear accelerator operating in the megavoltage regime produces a beam of x-rays by accelerating electrons and using them to create bremmstrahlung.  Such a device can be attached to some sort of flexible armature for positioning and outfitted with dose monitors and electronic feedback circuits, etc to make a radiation therapy device.  Other examples are manufactured Co-60 pellets, proton cyclotrons, etc.
is_a: OBI:0000968

[Term]
id: RTO:0000003
name: patient positioner
def: "A device that is used to position a patient during a health care process." []
comment: Such a device is  also often used to partially or completely immobilize the patient during the process.
is_a: OBI:0000968

